// Point diag_world_writer at the LOCAL matrix instead of the WORLD one.
//
// Run 21:49:45 killed the last inference-based approach. With the restore at all
// three write sites, PRE and A both read 0.1713 on every sample - our value is in
// the buffer everywhere WE run - and B at the tail still reads 0.114-0.681 with
// |clav-upper| 0.134-0.758 on the tick. So the engine rewrites element 48's LOCAL
// translation somewhere between our write sites and the tail, and the world matrix
// is composed from the stomped value.
//
// This file already recorded the same shape for ROTATIONS in the firearm era: our
// value present at d7380 ENTRY and the next dd7b0, yet the drawn arm 0.41 m wrong,
// so "the only uncovered part of the frame is inside d7380 itself, after our entry
// write". Six sessions of moving OUR write around have not found that moment.
//
// Stop guessing and ask the CPU. A hardware data breakpoint on the local
// translation reports the RIP of the storing instruction; RIP minus module base
// names the function. That is what worldwatch already does for world matrices -
// this only changes which of the two pointers it arms.
