// Localise the shoulder displacement in the PARENT CHAIN, by measuring the four
// bone separations whose rest lengths the rig already gives us. Pure read.
//
// This exists because the arithmetic does not close. hspine1 -> r_clavicle is
// 0.0853 and r_clavicle -> r_upperarm is 0.1718, so the shoulder can never sit
// more than 0.257 m from hspine1 no matter how those two joints rotate. The eye
// sits its own fixed offset from the same hspine1. A measured |eye - shoulder|
// of 1.11 m is therefore not reachable by ANY rotation of that chain - it needs
// a bone LENGTH to have changed, i.e. a translation being written, which is a
// different bug from "the game displaces the shoulder".
//
// So the separations, not the endpoints, are the measurement:
//   |hspine1 - clav|  must be 0.0853 forever
//   |clav - upper|    must be 0.1718 forever
//   |hspine1 - eye|   rest value unknown, but must be CONSTANT
// Whichever one moves names the joint. If none moves, 1.11 m came from a stale
// or wrong read rather than from the game, and the root cause is not the
// shoulder at all.
//
// Note the eye is the other candidate and was NOT cleared by the earlier
// measurement: per-tick step of 0.0000-0.0068 m proves the eye moves SMOOTHLY,
// not that it sits in the right place. A one-time displacement that then holds
// is exactly what that measurement cannot see.
#if !defined(DLVR_BETA_LEAN)   // BETA lean: constexpr false in boneblend.h (docs/BETA_CENSUS.md)
bool  DiagShoulderChain   = false;
#endif
// THE PARENT CHAIN ABOVE hspine1 - elements 0/1/2/3/4/5/6, never instrumented.
// [CHAIN] and [CHAIN L] cover clavicle -> upper arm and both read clean, while
// the DRAWN wrist walks off by up to 0.36 m. The error therefore enters through
// world_parent, and everything above hspine1 is the part nothing has ever looked
// at. See SpineChainProbe.
#if !defined(DLVR_BETA_LEAN)   // BETA lean: constexpr false in boneblend.h (docs/BETA_CENSUS.md)
bool  DiagSpineChain      = false;
#endif
