// THE DECISIVE EXPERIMENT for manual bow draw. FUN_1800D7380's decompression loop
// gates every entry on   *(short*)(map + i*0x10) != 0   AND   *(int*)(map+i*0x10+4) >= 0.
// Zero that short and the loop SKIPS that element entirely; because the copy-back
// at line 717 restores the snapshot, the element then keeps whatever was already
// there - i.e. our write from the previous frame. That is the engine's own "this
// bone is not animated" mechanism, per-element, so the LEFT arm can keep the bow
// animation while the RIGHT arm goes silent. Targets g_writeElement, which is
// driven by rig_arm_element (NOT rig_world_watch_elem - different knob).
//
// Strictly better than Block(i), which was disproven: its flag bit also clears the
// mesh element's render bit and makes the arm invisible.
