// The plausibility ceiling on |eye - element 48|, metres - now only the [SOLVE] line's IMPLAUSIBLE marker. Measured at a rock-steady
// 0.302 m with a melee weapon held, so 0.40 is still generous. 0.60 was the first
// value and it let a 0.496 m sample through, which is how the reference got
// poisoned on the bow's ramp.
float RigAnchorMaxM       = 0.40f;
// (rig_anchor_tol_m + the anchor-offset latch it defended: REMOVED 2026-10-07 - only rig_anchor_guard read the offset.)
// (rig_anchor_slew_max + rig_anchor_teleport_m: REMOVED 2026-10-07, audit section 2 - D-78 ruled the limiter out.)
// Ceiling on the elbow pole's world-up component. THE RIGHT ARM GOING UPSIDE
// DOWN. The pole is a blend of world-down and the hand axis, and past a threshold
// the blend crosses zero, taking the elbow above the shoulder and flipping the
// plane normal that both arm bones' roll is derived from. 0.0 = level with the
// shoulder at most, which is what a real elbow does with the hand at chest
// height. Raise toward 1 to restore the old unclamped behaviour.
float RigElbowPoleMaxUp   = 0.0f;
