// is why a single cone limit was wrong. Radial deviation is roughly a quarter of
// flexion, so one symmetric number either lets the hand fold sideways four times
// further than a hand can, or throttles flexion to a quarter of its range.
float RigWristFlexDeg        = 85.0f;   // palm inward,  75-90
float RigWristExtDeg         = 75.0f;   // back of hand, 60-90
float RigWristUlnarDeg       = 38.0f;   // toward pinky, 30-45
// >>> THE SHIPPED VALUE IS 30, NOT THE 18 BELOW, AND IT IS DELIBERATE. <<<
// [DEP: RigWristRadialDeg / rig_wrist_radial_deg] required-for=the wrist's radial stop
//      tree=LOADBEARING (shipped). STATE.md lists it under "WHAT IS SHIPPED AND WORKING.
//      Do not re-open these", evidence: "LEFT saturation 24.8% -> 6.5%" (INV-175). It is
//      the measured answer to INV-173's "THE RIGHT WRIST saturates its radial budget at
//      both ends". Changed 18 -> 30 on 2026-09-21 between 15:27 and 16:34; unbroken since.
//
// ⚠ THE "15-21" BELOW IS THE ANATOMICAL BAND, NOT THE SHIPPED VALUE, AND CONFLATING THE
