// band - question for Jay". It was neither. D-CFG-2 is WITHDRAWN; the trail is in
// docs/RIG_DEGENERACIES-2026-09-24.md section 13. The rig DELIBERATELY exceeds the
// anatomical radial limit here because saturating the stop was the worse artefact.
//
// rig_left_mirror_deviation=1 swaps the pairing (:6668-6670), so on the LEFT hand this 30
// lands on the ULNAR stop and rig_wrist_ulnar_deg's 38 on the RADIAL - which is why
// INV-175's evidence is a LEFT saturation number. ⚠ The wider stop does widen the band in
// which D-RIG-4's unstable-direction case passes a swing through rather than clipping it;
// that is a note about D-RIG-4, NOT a reason to revisit this value.
float RigWristRadialDeg      = 30.0f;   // DEFAULT 30 since 2026-10-01 (Jay's value, Tier B). Anatomical band 15-21.
