// ADDED 2026-09-14, AND IT CLOSES A HOLE THAT WAS READING AS A RESULT.
//
// The three checkpoints above all sample BEFORE the function they are named for
// does its work: kCpWriter fires at HookWriter's TOP, before g_trueWriter(ctx).
// So nothing has ever sampled the buffer AFTER FUN_1800DD7B0 ran - and
// FUN_1800DD7B0 is the function now suspected of dragging our write (INV-30).
//
// The 2026-09-14 baseline reads `next dd7b0: ours=3510 clob=0` on every driven bone.
// That looks exactly like "dd7b0 does not touch us" and means "we never looked."
// ABSENCE OF OUTPUT IS NOT INFORMATION - and this one was already being quoted.
