// Defined much further down, next to the rest of the matrix maths. Forward
// declared so the instrumentation can live here with the state it belongs to
// rather than being scattered to wherever the helpers happen to sit.
void Mat3Mul(const float* a, const float* b, float* out);
void Mat3Transpose(const float* m, float* out);
void Mtx34To3x3(const float* m, float* out);
// >>> INV-11 IS WHY THIS EXISTS, AND IT IS NOT OPTIONAL. <<<
// `hspine1`'s world basis scale reads UNIT on all 320 VR samples and ~0.4 in
// FLAT. That non-unit scale is precisely what made Mat3AngleBetween return a
// meaningless constant and VOID [ARMCOMP] v1 - its trace formula assumes an
// orthonormal basis. Any churn or divergence measure that fed raw bases into it
// would print a full, plausible, entirely fictional angle in flatscreen.
//
// So every basis is normalised COLUMN BY COLUMN before an angle is taken, and
// the scale actually observed is REPORTED by the caller rather than assumed
// away. Normalising also fixes distance: a 0.4-scaled basis would shrink every
// eye-local offset by 0.4 and the metres would be wrong.
//
// The 3x4 keeps its basis vectors in the COLUMNS (see Mtx34To3x3), so column c
// is { m[c], m[3+c], m[6+c] }.
//
// DEFINED HERE, not beside [RELCHURN] where the reasoning was first written:
// [HHCLOB] needs it 13,000 lines earlier, and a forward declaration in this
// region lands in the ANONYMOUS NAMESPACE and becomes a SECOND OVERLOAD - the
// same C2668 a VecLen forward declaration caused on 2026-09-22.
bool Mat3NormalizeCols(const float* in, float* out, float* lenOut3)
{
    for (int c = 0; c < 3; ++c) {
        const float x = in[c], y = in[3 + c], z = in[6 + c];
        const float len = sqrtf(x * x + y * y + z * z);
        lenOut3[c] = len;
        if (!(len > 1e-6f)) { return false; }   // also rejects NaN
        out[c]     = x / len;
        out[3 + c] = y / len;
        out[6 + c] = z / len;
    }
    return true;
}

